\description{
\code{access_wikiaves} authenticates with \href{https://www.wikiaves.com.br}{WikiAves},
which sits behind Cloudflare's bot protection and blocks plain \code{httr2}
requests with an HTTP 403 and a "Just a moment..." challenge page. This
function works around that by driving a real, visible Chromium-based
browser (Google Chrome, Chromium, or another compatible build) through
the Chrome DevTools Protocol (CDP): it launches the browser (or reuses
one already running) pointed at WikiAves, waits for Cloudflare's
JavaScript challenge to clear, and then extracts the resulting cookies
and the user agent string. The values are packed into a single
character string.

By default (\code{set_env = TRUE}) this string is also stored directly in
the \code{wikiaves_cookies} environment variable for the current R session,
which is what \code{\link[=query_wikiaves]{query_wikiaves()}} reads from by default -- so in the
common case, calling \code{access_wikiaves()} once is enough to authenticate
every subsequent \code{\link[=query_wikiaves]{query_wikiaves()}} call in the session without passing
\code{cookies} explicitly. See Details.

This function works on Linux, macOS, and Windows. On all three
platforms it will try to auto-detect a suitable browser and a writable
temporary directory if \code{chrome_bin} and \code{user_data_dir} are left at
their default (\code{NULL}); see Details.
}
